s":37.789,"e":37.858,"line":"c1","accent":false,"brk":false},{"w":"in","s":37.893,"e":37.939,"line":"c1","accent":false,"brk":false},{"w":"my","s":37.974,"e":38.044,"line":"c1","accent":false,"brk":false},{"w":"bio.","s":38.079,"e":38.526,"line":"c1","accent":true,"brk":false},{"w":"It's","s":38.565,"e":38.751,"line":"c1","accent":false,"brk":true},{"w":"called","s":38.797,"e":39.041,"line":"c1","accent":false,"brk":false},{"w":"Teyro.","s":39.111,"e":39.842,"line":"c1","accent":true,"brk":false}],"lines":[{"id":"h1","start":0.12,"end":4.599,"text":"Rereading your notes is one of the worst ways to study. Here are four things the research found instead."},{"id":"i1a","start":4.699,"end":9.277,"text":"First, a study from 2006. Students either reread a passage, or tested themselves on it."},{"id":"i1b","start":9.377,"end":13.24,"text":"One week later, the testers remembered sixty-one percent. The rereaders? Forty."},{"id":"i2","start":13.34,"end":20.433,"text":"Second, the rereaders felt more confident. Rereading feels like learning, because the words look familiar. Your brain mistakes I've seen this for I know this."},{"id":"i3","start":20.533,"end":26.047,"text":"Third, a review of 118 studies found practice tests beat the other ways of studying, again and again."},{"id":"i4","start":26.147,"end":31.344,"text":"And finally, feedback. When people checked the right answer straight after testing themselves, the benefit nearly doubled."},{"id":"s1","start":31.444,"end":34.534,"text":"So close the notes, quiz yourself, and check your answers right away."},{"id":"c1","start":34.634,"end":39.671,"text":"If you want lessons that make you do exactly that, a few minutes a day, the app is in my bio. It's called Teyro."}],"lip":{"amp":[0,0,0,0.002,0.05,0.999,1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1,1,0.779,1,1,1,1,0.931,1,1,0.863,0.855,0.889,0.917,0.813,0.767,0.066,0.803,0.486,0.839,0.828,0.643,1,1,0.866,0.924,0.561,0.352,1,1,0.89,0.633,1,1,1,0.855,0.693,0.478,0.423,0.11,1,1,0.989,1,1,0.818,0.599,0.368,